                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[From the <placeName>London</placeName> News
                        of <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-11-09">November 9,
                        1866</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>A deputation on the subject of the Atlantic and Pacific junction railway across
                    Nicaragua was received by Lord Stanley, at the Foreign Office, this afternoon.
                    The project was explained to Lord Stanley, in its various bearings, by Captain
                    Pim, Captain Maury, and Mr. Pollock. His lordship stated, in reply, that he
                    considered the matter one of great importance, and that he regarded it very
                    favorably, at the same time promising to give the documents laid before him his
                    careful attention, and to communicate fully with Captain Pim on the subject,
                    without delay.</p>
                <p>A telegram just received by the Varner Railway Company announces that the line
                    has been accepted by the government, and was opened yesterday to the public.</p>
            </div>
